# Chat 18 (directed coverage, decided 2026-11-14): 2:9 before the gate was ever fought, with the wagon bought, so
# the bugbears ask the 15 gold toll (0xAB64-0xAC4B) and the towers are still manned (0xA1C3, 0xA2E4: 0x4A77 bits
# 4 and 8 clear; the mage and the fighter, 0xA23F, 0xA372; the bugbears waiting inside the gate, 0xAD1F). The main
# line's checkpoint has the gate unfought too (0x4A77 = 0), but no wagon. Set by shortcut as a player who hasn't fought there has them:
# 0x4A77 = 96 (the gate seen, 0xAABB OR 32; the wagon bought, 0xB014 OR 64; nothing else), the alarm off (0x4A64
# = 0, as 0x9BA0 writes), the warnings not yet given (0x4A78 = 0) and the gate not taken (0x4AB9 = 0, a new game).
# Each event walked from the arrival ("fresh"): the other gate squares' warnings set 0x4A78 = 3 first otherwise,
# and the toll square then calls the party impostors (0xAB80).
rules playthrough.plan
start chat13a_latest/graveyard
shortcut flag 4A77 set 96 gate seen and wagon bought, never fought (2:9 0xAABB, 0xB014)
shortcut flag 4A64 set 0 no alarm (2:9 0x9BA0)
shortcut flag 4A78 set 0 no warnings yet (a new game)
shortcut flag 4AB9 set 0 the gate not taken (a new game)
travel 2:9
expect 2:9
cover 2:9 60 all fresh
status
stop
